{
  "id": "positivenegative-asymmetry",
  "term": "positive–negative asymmetry",
  "definition": "Positive–negative asymmetry is a pattern in comparison judgments in which negative changes or features influence perceived similarity more strongly than positive ones. In the source context, adding negative qualities to a candidate altered judgments of similarity to an ideal candidate more than changing positive qualities did.",
